WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.681 --> 00:00:03.152
- [Voiceover] In 1954,
Steve and Gayle Henson

00:00:03.152 --> 00:00:06.654
bought a ranch in California
called Sweetwater Ranch.

00:00:06.654 --> 00:00:10.590
The area they loved,
the name not so much.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:14.007
So they changed it to Hidden Valley Ranch.

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:18.589
I think you can guess where this is going.

00:00:21.607 --> 00:00:24.480
Ranch dressing is called ranch dressing

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.876
because it was made on a ranch.

00:00:27.876 --> 00:00:29.460
So here's the story, it's a quickie.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.235
Steve was working in Alaska, he had a crew

00:00:32.235 --> 00:00:33.685
and for lunch he would whip up

00:00:33.685 --> 00:00:37.566
this buttermilk dressing for
them, which they all loved.

00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:40.736
Cut to 1954, we're back
at Hidden Valley Ranch,

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:43.696
Gayle and Steve have opened
their ranch up to guests

00:00:43.696 --> 00:00:45.862
and at the end of the day,
everyone would sit around

00:00:45.862 --> 00:00:49.242
and Steve would serve his ranch dressing.

00:00:49.242 --> 00:00:51.104
Okay, here was the original recipe.

00:00:51.104 --> 00:00:53.629
Buttermilk, mayo, sour
cream, dried parsley,

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:56.133
dried onion, dried
garlic, salt and pepper.

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.178
And people were all like, oh my God

00:00:58.178 --> 00:01:00.162
I love your ranch dressing.

00:01:00.162 --> 00:01:01.962
So Steve and Gayle started selling it.

00:01:01.962 --> 00:01:03.869
It began as mail order for 75 cents

00:01:03.869 --> 00:01:07.183
they would send a pack of the
flavoring and it took off.

00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:10.688
In 1973, Clorox came in and
bought it for the big bucks,

00:01:10.688 --> 00:01:13.274
eight million of them
and they began selling it

00:01:13.274 --> 00:01:16.403
as Hidden Valley Ranch Dressing.

00:01:16.403 --> 00:01:18.933
Move up into the 90's
and ranch is being named

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:21.079
the most popular dressing in America.

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:24.940
And there it is, ranch
dressing, it came from a ranch.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.357
What do you know?

